    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per hour</p><hr><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">You can leverage the momentum of one creature you brush away to topple another nearby. When you successfully Shove or Trip a creature, you can attempt your choice of a Shove or Trip check against one creature your original target is adjacent to at the end of your previous attempt. If you become a Master in Athletics, you can attempt a Shove or Trip attempt against two adjacent creatures from the original target, or four if you become Legendary, using the same maneuver for all targets and only increasing your multi-attack penalty for the number of attempts you make after all the maneuvers are made.</span></p>"
